    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0332" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–2848</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d249-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-28">June 28, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Consul General has the honor to transmit a copy of a memorandum prepared by
                    Vice Consul Allen C. Siebens on June 24, 1948, setting forth <hi
                        rendition="#italic">inter alia</hi> information gleaned from Japanese
                    sources on the receipt by Manchurian communists of supplies of probable Soviet
                    origin.</p>
                <p>While the information set forth in the memorandum on the above-mentioned is
                    largely circumstantial and pertains to the movement of goods a year ago, it
                    nevertheless substantiates to some slight degree the bruited supply of arms and
                    military equipment by the Soviet Union to the Manchurian communists.</p>


                <xi:include href="d249-a1.xml" xpointer="d249-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="50" type="source" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Consul General without covering
                    despatch; received July 23.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
